{"name":"Tallow","hex":"#a39977","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tallow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard animal fat obtained from suet, etc.; used in cooking as well as to make candles, soap and lubricants."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grease or smear with tallow.","To cause to have a large quantity of tallow; to fatten."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tallow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tallow","blocks":[{"text":"Tallow is a rendered form of beef, pork, or mutton suet, primarily made up of triglycerides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Tallow-beef_suet_after_rendering.jpg/330px-Tallow-beef_suet_after_rendering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tallow","wikidata":"Q863266"},{"title":"Tallow (Parliament of Ireland constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Tallow was a constituency represented in the Irish House of Commons until 1800, centred on Tallow, County Waterford."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Dublin_Penny_Journal_1834-11-22_Lisfinny_Castle_by_E._Heyden.png/330px-Dublin_Penny_Journal_1834-11-22_Lisfinny_Castle_by_E._Heyden.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tallow_(Parliament_of_Ireland_constituency)","wikidata":"Q7680173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Tallow_Ad.jpg/330px-Tallow_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Tallow_Ad.jpg/330px-Tallow_Ad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 1883 ad soliciting tallow from butchers and graziers for soap production in the Hawaii newspaper The Daily Bulletin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATallow_Ad.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum